  - semi-rigid boundary condition
abstract: >-
  A MATLAB framework for the two-degree-of-freedom vortex-induced vibration of
  long flexible cylinders in non-uniform currents.  In-line and cross-flow
  displacements and sectional rotations are solved as primary variables of a
  mixed Timoshenko beam formulation, which allows bending moment, shear force
  and beam-based stress indicators to be recovered directly from the
  displacement-rotation fields.  Pinned, semi-rigid and clamped supports are
  represented by an elastic-boundary formulation, and vibration-induced
  axial-tension feedback is introduced through centreline stretching.  The
  package contains an open parameter interface and a selectable
  post-processing layer, with the core numerical algorithms distributed as
  protected MATLAB P-code.
